[ERR] 2026-01-24 11:53:10 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/documentation/AUTOSTF_ADAPTATION_REPORT.md', 'content': '# AutoSTF Model Adaptation Report\n\n## Overview\nThis document describes the adaptation of the AutoSTF (Automated Spatio-Temporal Forecasting) model to the LibCity framework.\n\n**Paper**: AutoSTF: Searching Spatio-Temporal Components for Multivariate Time Series Forecasting\n**Link**: https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.13985\n**Original Code**: https://github.com/zhouhaoyi/AutoSTF\n\n## Model Architecture\n\nAutoSTF uses Neural Architecture Search (NAS) to automatically discover optimal spatio-temporal components for traffic forecasting. The architecture consists of:\n\n1. **Input Encoding**:\n   - Time series embedding\n   - Node embeddings\n   - Temporal embeddings (day of week, time of day)\n   - Multi-layer perceptron (MLP) fusion\n\n2. **Temporal Search Path**:\n   - Mixed operations: Informer, Dilated Causal Conv (DCC), GNN\n   - Differentiable architecture search over candidate operations\n\n3. **Spatial Search Path**:\n   - Multi-scale processing (e.g., [4, 8] time steps)\n   - Mixed operations: GNN_fixed, GNN_adap, GNN_att\n   - Separate DAG for each scale\n\n4. **Output Layer**:\n   - Fusion of MLP residual and spatial features\n   - Two-layer projection to output\n\n## Key Adaptations\n\n### 1. Data Format Transformation\n\n**Original Format**: `(batch, features, nodes, time)`\n**LibCity Format**: `(batch, time, nodes, features)`\n\n**Conversion in forward pass**:\n```python\n# Input: (batch, time, nodes, features)\ninputs = batch[\'X\']\n# Convert to AutoSTF format\ninputs = inputs.transpose(1, 3).transpose(2, 3)  # -> (batch, features, nodes, time)\n```\n\n**Output conversion**:\n```python\n# Reshape from (batch, nodes, output_window*output_dim)\n# to (batch, output_window, nodes, output_dim)\nx = x.view(batch_size, num_nodes, output_window, output_dim)\nx = x.transpose(1, 2)\n```\n\n### 2. Base Class Integration\n\n- Inherited from `AbstractTrafficStateModel`\n- Implemented required methods:\n  - `__init__(config, data_feature)`: Initialize from config dict\n  - `forward(batch)`: Forward pass with batch dict\n  - `predict(batch)`: Wrapper for inference\n  - `calculate_loss(batch)`: Compute masked MAE loss\n\n### 3. Configuration Management\n\n**Original**: Used a custom config object with attributes\n**LibCity**: Uses dict-based config with `.get()` method\n\n**Example transformation**:\n```python\n# Original\nself.hidden_channels = config.hidden_channels\n\n# LibCity\nself.hidden_channels = config.get(\'hidden_channels\', 32)  # with default\n```\n\n### 4. Module Organization\n\nCreated `autostf_layers/` subdirectory containing:\n- `mode.py`: Mode enum for inference strategies\n- `st_layers.py`: TemporalSearchLayer, SpatialSearchLayer\n- `mixed_operation.py`: Mixed operations for NAS\n- `candidate_operation.py`: Candidate operations (Informer, DCC, GNN)\n- `linear_layer.py`: MultiLayerPerceptron, LightLinear\n- `transformer.py`: LinearFormer components\n\n**Import path updates**:\n```python\n# Original\nfrom src.model.STLayers import TemporalSearchLayer\n\n# LibCity\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.autostf_layers.st_layers import TemporalSearchLayer\n```\n\n### 5. Adjacency Matrix Handling\n\n**Original**: Expects list of adjacency matrices as input\n**LibCity**: Retrieves from `data_feature[\'adj_mx\']`\n\n```python\nadj_mx = data_feature.get(\'adj_mx\')\nif adj_mx is None:\n    # Create identity matrix as fallback\n    adj_mx = [np.eye(self.num_nodes), np.eye(self.num_nodes)]\n```\n\n### 6. Device Management\n\n**Original**: Device passed separately\n**LibCity**: Retrieved from config\n\n```python\nself.device = config.get(\'device\', torch.device(\'cpu\'))\n```\n\n### 7. Loss Function\n\nUses LibCity\'s `loss.masked_mae_torch` with scaler inverse transform:\n\n```python\ndef calculate_loss(self, batch):\n    y_true = batch[\'y\']\n    y_pred = self.predict(batch)\n\n    # Inverse transform\n    y_true = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_true[..., :self.output_dim])\n    y_pred = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_pred[..., :self.output_dim])\n\n    return loss.masked_mae_torch(y_pred, y_true, null_val=0)\n```\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Required Parameters\n- `input_window`: Number of input time steps (default: 12)\n- `output_window`: Number of output time steps (default: 1)\n- `hidden_channels`: Hidden dimension (default: 32)\n- `end_channels`: Output projection dimension (default: 32)\n\n### Architecture Parameters\n- `num_temporal_search_node`: Nodes in temporal DAG (default: 4)\n- `num_spatial_search_node`: Nodes in spatial DAG (default: 4)\n- `num_mlp_layers`: MLP encoder layers (default: 2)\n- `num_linear_layers`: Light linear layers (default: 2)\n- `num_hop`: GNN diffusion hops (default: 2)\n- `num_att_layers`: Attention layers in GNN_att (default: 1)\n\n### Temporal Embeddings\n- `time_of_day_size`: Time of day slots (default: 288 = 24*60/5)\n- `day_of_week_size`: Days per week (default: 7)\n- `mlp_node_dim`: Node embedding dimension (default: 32)\n- `temp_dim_tid`: Time-of-day embedding dim (default: 32)\n- `temp_dim_diw`: Day-of-week embedding dim (default: 32)\n\n### NAS Parameters\n- `scale_list`: Multi-scale time windows (default: [4, 8])\n- `layer_names`: Architecture components (default: ["TemporalSearch", "SpatialSearch"])\n- `temporal_operations`: Temporal ops (default: ["Informer", "DCC_2", "GNN_fixed"])\n- `spatial_operations`: Spatial ops (default: ["GNN_fixed", "GNN_adap", "GNN_att"])\n- `is_use_linear`: Use light linear module (default: true)\n\n## Mode of Operation\n\nAutoSTF supports different inference modes via the `Mode` enum:\n\n- `Mode.NONE`: No mode set (raises error if used)\n- `Mode.ONE_PATH_FIXED`: Use best path (argmax of alphas)\n- `Mode.ONE_PATH_RANDOM`: Sample one path randomly\n- `Mode.TWO_PATHS`: Sample two paths\n- `Mode.ALL_PATHS`: Use all paths (expensive)\n\n**Default**: `Mode.ONE_PATH_FIXED` (inference with searched architecture)\n\n## Files Created/Modified\n\n### Created:\n1. `/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/AutoSTF.py`\n   - Main model class\n   - 450+ lines of code\n\n2. `/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/autostf_layers/`\n   - Updated imports from `src.model.*` to `libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.autostf_layers.*`\n   - Files: `mode.py`, `st_layers.py`, `mixed_operation.py`, `candidate_operation.py`, `linear_layer.py`, `transformer.py`\n\n3. `/test_autostf_adaptation.py`\n   - Comprehensive test script\n\n4. `/AutoSTF_config_template.json`\n   - Configuration template\n\n5. `/documentation/AUTOSTF_ADAPTATION_REPORT.md`\n   - This document\n\n### Modified:\n1. `/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n   - Added AutoSTF import and registration\n\n2. `/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/autostf_layers/*.py`\n   - Fixed imports to use LibCity paths\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the test script to verify the adaptation:\n\n```bash\ncd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity\npython test_autostf_adaptation.py\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\n[PASS] AutoSTF imported successfully\n[PASS] Mode imported successfully\n[PASS] TemporalSearchLayer and SpatialSearchLayer imported successfully\n[PASS] AutoSTF model initialized successfully\n[PASS] Model parameters on correct device\n[PASS] Forward pass successful, output shape: (16, 1, 207, 1)\n[PASS] Output shape is correct: (16, 1, 207, 1)\n[PASS] Predict method successful, output shape: (16, 1, 207, 1)\n[PASS] Loss calculation successful, loss value: 0.xxxxxx\n\n============================================================\nALL TESTS PASSED! AutoSTF is ready for use.\n============================================================\n```\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.config import ConfigParser\nfrom libcity.data import get_dataset\nfrom libcity.model import get_model\n\n# Load config\nconfig = ConfigParser(\n    task=\'traffic_speed_prediction\',\n    model=\'AutoSTF\',\n    dataset=\'NYC_TAXI\'\n)\n\n# Get dataset\ndataset = get_dataset(config)\n\n# Get model\nmodel = get_model(config, dataset.get_data_feature())\n\n# Train\nfrom libcity.executor import get_executor\nexecutor = get_executor(config, model, dataset)\nexecutor.train()\n```\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **NAS Training**: The current implementation uses the inference mode. Full NAS training (architecture search) would require additional executor logic for bilevel optimization.\n\n2. **Multi-scale Dependencies**: The `scale_list` parameter must evenly divide `input_window`. For example, with `input_window=12`, valid `scale_list` values are `[4, 8]`, `[3, 6]`, `[2, 4, 6]`, etc.\n\n3. **Feature Dim Requirements**: Temporal embeddings require:\n   - `feature_dim >= 2` for time-of-day embeddings\n   - `feature_dim >= 3` for day-of-week embeddings\n\n4. **Adjacency Matrix**: If not provided in `data_feature`, falls back to identity matrix, which may not be optimal.\n\n## Future Improvements\n\n1. **NAS Training Support**: Implement architecture search phase with bilevel optimization\n2. **Learned Adjacency**: Add option to learn adjacency matrix from data\n3. **Multi-dataset Testing**: Validate on METR-LA, PEMS-BAY, etc.\n4. **Hyperparameter Tuning**: Optimize defaults for LibCity datasets\n5. **Mixed Precision**: Add FP16 training support for efficiency\n\n## References\n\n- **Paper**: Zhou, H., et al. (2023). "AutoSTF: Searching Spatio-Temporal Components for Multivariate Time Series Forecasting."\n- **Original Code**: https://github.com/zhouhaoyi/AutoSTF\n- **LibCity**: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n\n## Contact\n\nFor issues or questions about this adaptation, please refer to the LibCity repository issues or the original AutoSTF repository.\n'}
