ts\n\n## Files Modified\n\n### 1. Model Registry\n**Path**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n- Added: `from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.AutoSTF import AutoSTF`\n- Added: `"AutoSTF"` to `__all__` list\n\n## Key Adaptations\n\n### Data Format Conversion\n- **Input**: LibCity `(batch, time, nodes, features)` → AutoSTF `(batch, features, nodes, time)`\n- **Output**: AutoSTF format → LibCity `(batch, time, nodes, features)`\n\n### Configuration Management\n- Converted from attribute-based config to dict-based config with `.get()` method\n- Added default values for all parameters\n\n### Base Class Integration\n- Inherits from `AbstractTrafficStateModel`\n- Uses LibCity\'s loss functions (`masked_mae_torch`)\n- Integrates with LibCity\'s scaler for normalization\n\n### Import Path Updates\n- Changed all `from src.model.*` imports to `from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.autostf_layers.*`\n\n## Model Architecture\n\nAutoSTF uses Neural Architecture Search (NAS) to discover optimal spatio-temporal components:\n\n1. **Input Encoding**\n   - Time series embeddings\n   - Node embeddings\n   - Temporal embeddings (time-of-day, day-of-week)\n   - Multi-layer perceptron fusion\n\n2. **Temporal Search Path**\n   - Candidate operations: Informer, DCC, GNN_fixed\n   - Differentiable architecture search\n\n3. **Spatial Search Path**\n   - Multi-scale processing (configurable via `scale_list`)\n   - Candidate operations: GNN_fixed, GNN_adap, GNN_att\n   - Separate DAG for each scale\n\n4. **Output Layer**\n   - Fusion of MLP and spatial residuals\n   - Two-layer projection to predictions\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Essential\n- `input_window`: 12 (number of input timesteps)\n- `output_window`: 1 (number of prediction timesteps)\n- `hidden_channels`: 32 (hidden dimension)\n- `end_channels`: 32 (output projection dimension)\n\n### Architecture\n- `num_temporal_search_node`: 4 (temporal DAG nodes)\n- `num_spatial_search_node`: 4 (spatial DAG nodes)\n- `scale_list`: [4, 8] (multi-scale time windows)\n- `temporal_operations`: ["Informer", "DCC_2", "GNN_fixed"]\n- `spatial_operations`: ["GNN_fixed", "GNN_adap", "GNN_att"]\n\n### Embeddings\n- `time_of_day_size`: 288 (24*60/5 for 5-min intervals)\n- `day_of_week_size`: 7\n- `mlp_node_dim`: 32\n- `temp_dim_tid`: 32 (time-of-day embedding)\n- `temp_dim_diw`: 32 (day-of-week embedding)\n\n## Testing Instructions\n\n```bash\ncd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity\npython test_autostf_adaptation.py\n```\n\nExpected output includes:\n- ✅ All imports successful\n- ✅ Model initialization successful\n- ✅ Forward pass with correct output shape\n- ✅ Loss calculation successful\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.config import ConfigParser\nfrom libcity.data import get_dataset\nfrom libcity.model import get_model\nfrom libcity.executor import get_executor\n\n# Load configuration\nconfig = ConfigParser(\n    task=\'traffic_speed_prediction\',\n    model=\'AutoSTF\',\n    dataset=\'METR_LA\'\n)\n\n# Get dataset\ndataset = get_dataset(config)\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = get_model(config, dataset.get_data_feature())\n\n# Train\nexecutor = get_executor(config, model, dataset)\nexecutor.train()\n\n# Evaluate\nexecutor.evaluate()\n```\n\n## Inference Modes\n\nAutoSTF supports multiple inference strategies via `Mode` enum:\n\n- `Mode.ONE_PATH_FIXED`: Use best path (default, recommended)\n- `Mode.ONE_PATH_RANDOM`: Sample one path randomly\n- `Mode.TWO_PATHS`: Sample two paths\n- `Mode.ALL_PATHS`: Use all paths (expensive)\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **NAS Training**: Current implementation focuses on inference. Full architecture search requires additional executor logic.\n\n2. **Scale Constraints**: `scale_list` values must evenly divide `input_window`\n\n3. **Feature Requirements**:\n   - `feature_dim >= 2` for time-of-day embeddings\n   - `feature_dim >= 3` for day-of-week embeddings\n\n4. **Adjacency Matrix**: Falls back to identity matrix if not provided\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. ✅ **Verify Imports**: Run test script to ensure all imports work\n2. ⏭️ **Integration Testing**: Test with actual LibCity datasets (METR_LA, PEMS_BAY)\n3. ⏭️ **Hyperparameter Tuning**: Optimize defaults for different datasets\n4. ⏭️ **NAS Training**: Implement architecture search phase (optional)\n\n## Performance Expectations\n\nBased on the original paper:\n- **METR-LA**: MAE ~2.5-2.7, RMSE ~5.0-5.5\n- **PEMS-BAY**: MAE ~1.3-1.5, RMSE ~3.0-3.5\n- **Training Time**: ~2-4 hours per 100 epochs (GPU dependent)\n\n## File Paths Reference\n\nAll paths are absolute from the project root `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/`:\n\n- **Model**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/AutoSTF.py`\n- **Layers**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/autostf_layers/`\n- **Registry**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n- **Test**: `test_autostf_adaptation.py`\n- **Config**: `AutoSTF_config_template.json`\n- **Docs**: `documentation/AUTOSTF_ADAPTATION_REPORT.md`\n\n## References\n\n- **Paper**: https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.13985\n- **Original Code**: https://github.com/zhouhaoyi/AutoSTF\n- **LibCity Framework**: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n\n---\n\n**Status**: Ready for integration testing and deployment\n**Date**: 2026-01-24\n**Adapted by**: Model Adaptation Agent (Claude)\n'}
