_dim\'] = 1\n\n# If traffic flow + time-of-day:\nconfig[\'feature_dim\'] = 2\n\n# If traffic flow + time-of-day + day-of-week:\nconfig[\'feature_dim\'] = 3\n```\n\n### Issue 3: No Adjacency Matrix\n**Warning**: Using identity matrix\n**Solution**: Provide proper adjacency matrix in `data_feature`\n```python\ndata_feature[\'adj_mx\'] = [adj_forward, adj_backward]\n```\n\n## Performance Tuning\n\n### For Larger Datasets (500+ nodes)\n```python\nconfig.update({\n    \'hidden_channels\': 64,\n    \'num_temporal_search_node\': 3,\n    \'num_spatial_search_node\': 3,\n    \'batch_size\': 16\n})\n```\n\n### For Longer Sequences (24+ timesteps)\n```python\nconfig.update({\n    \'input_window\': 24,\n    \'scale_list\': [6, 12],\n    \'num_linear_layers\': 3\n})\n```\n\n### For Limited Memory\n```python\nconfig.update({\n    \'hidden_channels\': 16,\n    \'batch_size\': 8,\n    \'is_use_linear\': False\n})\n```\n\n## Architecture Variants\n\n### Temporal-Only\n```python\nconfig[\'layer_names\'] = [\'TemporalSearch\']\n```\n\n### Spatial-Only\n```python\nconfig[\'layer_names\'] = [\'SpatialSearch\']\n```\n\n### Full Model (Default)\n```python\nconfig[\'layer_names\'] = [\'TemporalSearch\', \'SpatialSearch\']\n```\n\n## Operation Sets\n\n### Temporal Operations\n- `Informer`: Attention-based temporal modeling\n- `DCC_2`: Dilated causal convolution (dilation=2)\n- `GNN_fixed`: Fixed-adjacency graph convolution\n\n### Spatial Operations\n- `GNN_fixed`: Fixed adjacency graph\n- `GNN_adap`: Adaptive adjacency (learned)\n- `GNN_att`: Attention-based spatial dependencies\n\n### Custom Operation Set\n```python\nconfig.update({\n    \'temporal_operations\': [\'Informer\', \'DCC_2\'],  # Exclude GNN\n    \'spatial_operations\': [\'GNN_adap\', \'GNN_att\']  # Exclude fixed\n})\n```\n\n## Mode Selection\n\n### During Training\n```python\n# Use default mode (no need to set)\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n```\n\n### During Inference\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.autostf_layers.mode import Mode\n\n# Fixed architecture (fastest)\nmodel._mode = Mode.ONE_PATH_FIXED\npredictions = model.predict(batch)\n\n# Ensemble of two paths (better accuracy, slower)\nmodel._mode = Mode.TWO_PATHS\npredictions = model.predict(batch)\n```\n\n## Debugging Tips\n\n### 1. Check Input Shape\n```python\nprint(f"Input shape: {batch[\'X\'].shape}")\n# Should be: (batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)\n```\n\n### 2. Check Output Shape\n```python\noutput = model.forward(batch)\nprint(f"Output shape: {output.shape}")\n# Should be: (batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)\n```\n\n### 3. Monitor Layer Dimensions\n```python\n# Add this in forward() to debug\nprint(f"After temporal: {x_t.shape}")\nprint(f"After spatial: {x.shape}")\nprint(f"Final output: {output.shape}")\n```\n\n### 4. Verify Device Placement\n```python\nprint(f"Model device: {next(model.parameters()).device}")\nprint(f"Input device: {batch[\'X\'].device}")\n```\n\n## Integration with LibCity\n\n### Standard Training Pipeline\n```python\nfrom libcity.config import ConfigParser\nfrom libcity.data import get_dataset\nfrom libcity.model import get_model\nfrom libcity.executor import get_executor\n\nconfig = ConfigParser(\n    task=\'traffic_speed_prediction\',\n    model=\'AutoSTF\',\n    dataset=\'METR_LA\',\n    config_file=\'AutoSTF_config_template.json\'\n)\n\ndataset = get_dataset(config)\nmodel = get_model(config, dataset.get_data_feature())\nexecutor = get_executor(config, model, dataset)\n\nexecutor.train()\nexecutor.evaluate()\n```\n\n### Custom Training Loop\n```python\noptimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.001)\n\nfor epoch in range(num_epochs):\n    for batch in train_loader:\n        optimizer.zero_grad()\n        loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n        loss.backward()\n        optimizer.step()\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Start Small**: Test with small `hidden_channels` (16-32) before scaling up\n2. **Scale Alignment**: Always ensure `scale_list` values divide `input_window` evenly\n3. **Feature Matching**: Match `feature_dim` to your actual data features\n4. **Device Consistency**: Keep all tensors on the same device\n5. **Gradient Clipping**: Use gradient clipping for stable training\n   ```python\n   torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), max_norm=5.0)\n   ```\n\n## Troubleshooting Checklist\n\n- [ ] All imports successful?\n- [ ] Config contains required parameters?\n- [ ] `input_window` divisible by `scale_list` values?\n- [ ] `feature_dim` matches input tensor last dimension?\n- [ ] Adjacency matrix provided or using default?\n- [ ] All tensors on same device?\n- [ ] Batch dict contains \'X\' and \'y\' keys?\n- [ ] Input shape is `(batch, time, nodes, features)`?\n\n## Further Reading\n\n- Full documentation: `documentation/AUTOSTF_ADAPTATION_REPORT.md`\n- Configuration template: `AutoSTF_config_template.json`\n- Test script: `test_autostf_adaptation.py`\n- Original paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.13985\n'}

